Since this is dependent on your specific circumstances and what information you have provided so far, please reply with whether you are applying to **get a replacement**, **get a corrected** card, or if you already possess an original card. Additionally, please let us know which of the following categories might apply:
[1] If you need to prove their U.S. citizenship;
[2] If you need to establish their foreign birth certificate within 10 days of application;
[3] If they have lived outside the United States for an extended period; or
[4] If they are requesting proof that they do not currently have a Social Security number (e.g., due to prior absence).

Greetings and welcome today! I am here to walk you through exactly how to activate your **Service Members' Group Life Insurance (SGLI)** benefits, a crucial program designed to help eligible service members afford health insurance for themselves and their dependents while they serve or are on active duty.

To get you started, there is one simple question at the very end of this answer: **"How do I get sGLI?"**

### Step 1: Meet Your Qualifications
First, please ensure that **at least one** of the following conditions applies to your current status or training schedule:
*   You are currently an active-duty member of the Army, Navy, Air Force, Marines, or Coast Guard;
*   You are a commissioned officer in the U.S. Public Health Service (USPHS) or NOAA;
*   You are attending a military academy as a cadet or midshipman;
*   You are participating in ROTC (Ready Reserve or National Guard members scheduled for at least 12 periods of inactive training per year, or those on authorized service);
*   You are on active duty with the Army, Navy, Air Force, Marine Corps, Coast Guard, or NOAA.

> **[p947]** Servicemembers' Group Life Insurance (SGLI) | Veterans Affairs

